# ReconDesk Backend — Cursor Rules

## Rule Registry
When adding any new GST logic rule, ALWAYS use the rule registry in app/rules/.
Never put matching or ITC logic directly in rule files — only metadata.

Pattern to follow every time:
REGISTRY.register(RuleDefinition(
    id          = "ITC_021",        # next unused ID in this file
    name        = "Short name",
    category    = RuleCategory.ITC,
    severity    = RuleSeverity.HIGH,
    description = "One sentence plain English.",
    gst_ref     = "Section X CGST Act",
    applies_to  = ["purchase_register"],
    tags        = ["itc", "reversal"],
))

File to edit by prefix:
- MAT_ → app/rules/matching.py
- ITC_ → app/rules/itc.py
- NRM_ → app/rules/normalization.py
- PRD_, SUP_, RPT_, TDS_ → app/rules/period.py
- DEC_ → app/rules/decision.py

Severity guide:
- CRITICAL → tax liability, notice risk, wrongful ITC
- HIGH → ITC loss risk, reversal risk, blocked credit
- MEDIUM → process quality, data warnings
- LOW → informational, parser behaviour

After adding rules, verify count with:
python3 -c "from app.rules import REGISTRY; print('Total rules:', REGISTRY.count)"

## General Backend Rules
- Always run: python3 -c "from app.main import app; print('OK')" before Railway deploy
- Auth imports: use supabase_auth not gotrue
- Backend path: /Users/omkarkadam/Documents/ReconDesk/recondesk-backend
- Celery start: celery -A app.celery_app worker --loglevel=info
